{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog", "label": "dead-drop Changelog", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_fyrlabs_dead_drop", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop package", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shipped as one package with subpaths (/sdk, /runtime, /core, /protocol, /cli, /transports/<name>) instead of ten packages."}, {"id": "changelog_transport_sdk", "label": "@fyrlabs/dead-drop-transport-sdk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Versions independently (1.0.0 at 0.2.0) because the contract is settled; kept separate so a third-party adapter does not depend on the whole runtime."}, {"id": "changelog_deaddroperror", "label": "DeadDropError (symbol brand check)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in transport-sdk because adapters must throw it and the transport manager reads its retryable flag. DeadDropError.is checks a Symbol.for key, not instanceof, so errors from two copies of transport-sdk are still recognised; otherwise UNAUTHORIZED got re-wrapped as retryable INTERNAL and retried forever."}, {"id": "changelog_eslint_layering", "label": "eslint no-restricted-imports layering rule", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces package boundaries after consolidation: protocol imports nothing above it, core never names a transport, a transport sees only protocol and transport SDK."}, {"id": "changelog_conformance_suite", "label": "Transport conformance suite", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.6.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "transport-sdk 1.1.0 checks that listing a prefix returns nested keys; an adapter that did not would report every queue as empty."}, {"id": "changelog_streaming_responses", "label": "Streaming response bodies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.16.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lets SSE and never-ending bodies work and large files avoid fitting in memory on both peers. Opt in per exposure with streaming.enabled. A caller that stops reading stops the sender. Replaces the 0.1.0 limitation of whole buffered responses capped at 32 MiB."}, {"id": "changelog_response_cap_32mib", "label": "Buffered responses capped at 32 MiB", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_proxy_mode", "label": "Proxy mode (ddrop expose / ddrop connect)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_content_encoding_fix", "label": "content-encoding stripping for proxied targets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.15.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decompressed bytes were still labelled gzip, causing ERR_CONTENT_DECODING_FAILED. Asking the target not to compress costs nothing on the wire because frames are already compressed a layer down."}, {"id": "changelog_adaptive_polling", "label": "Adaptive polling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.15.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A peer awaiting a reply no longer backs off to 15s (18s to 5s per request on a local git remote); a peer with nothing outstanding still backs off so a quiet workspace costs no more."}, {"id": "changelog_key_rotation", "label": "ddrop rotate (per-peer key wrapping)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.13.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Removing a peer no longer requires distributing a new shared secret: a new key is wrapped for each peer that may still read. Earlier messages stay readable."}, {"id": "changelog_peer_enrollment", "label": "Peer enrollment and approval (ddrop peer list/approve/revoke)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.13.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "enrollment.requireApproval is off by default, for users who do not trust shared storage. Approval records the fingerprint so a peer whose key changes loses approval instead of inheriting it."}, {"id": "changelog_ddrop_expose_ux", "label": "ddrop expose name inference and connect hint", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.12.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A directory names the exposure after itself; --target still needs --name because a url has no obvious name."}, {"id": "changelog_config_validation", "label": "Config validation (polling, policy, retry, breaker, REPLACE-ME)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.12.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unknown keys and wrong types used to be accepted and then silently do nothing; start-up now fails naming the field."}, {"id": "changelog_parallel_policy", "label": "policy.mode parallel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.11.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sends every message and beacon to all transports for peers that cannot all reach the same ones; costs a write (a commit and push on git) per transport per message. Was previously accepted but ignored."}, {"id": "changelog_inbox_orphan_cleanup", "label": "Orphaned inbox cleanup (inboxOrphanMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.10.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mail for departed peers was never reclaimed (60 MB in one trial repo). Deleted only when older than 7 days AND the recipient stopped publishing presence, so a briefly offline peer keeps its mail."}, {"id": "changelog_presence_beacons", "label": "Presence beacons", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.3.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only one published at a time and abandoned once too old, so a slow backend is not pushed into failing by its own presence records."}, {"id": "changelog_ddrop_init", "label": "ddrop init (--root, --github, --secret)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.4.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes a working config: generated secret file, explicit peer id to avoid hostname collisions, REPLACE-ME for the shared location. --secret - reads stdin to keep the secret out of shell history."}, {"id": "changelog_git_compaction", "label": "Git data branch compaction (compactAfterCommits)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.8.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Past 500 commits the branch is replaced by one commit so joining stays fast and repos avoid host size limits. Disable on force-push-protected branches."}, {"id": "changelog_ddrop_dashboard", "label": "ddrop dashboard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.7.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read-only, starts no runtime, reads the same control socket as ddrop status. Run it only while looking because any local process can read workspace metadata from the port."}, {"id": "changelog_control_socket", "label": "Control socket (Unix socket / named pipe)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Falls back to a short hashed path under the temp dir because Unix socket paths cannot exceed 104 bytes; runtime and client derive it the same way."}, {"id": "changelog_ddrop_queues", "label": "ddrop queues / client.queues()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.6.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads object keys only, decrypting and consuming nothing."}, {"id": "changelog_ddrop_discover", "label": "ddrop discover / client.peers()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.6.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exits 1 naming the failed transport so an unreachable workspace no longer looks empty."}, {"id": "changelog_workspace_tuning", "label": "Workspace tuning (concurrency, healthIntervalMs, presenceIntervalMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.5.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "concurrency removes head-of-line blocking at the cost of ordering; health and presence intervals trade freshness against API calls or commits on github/git."}, {"id": "changelog_request_timeout", "label": "Request timeout bounds whole request", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.3.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Previously only guarded the reply, so a 15s request could wait two minutes while sends failed. Raising retry.maxAttempts alone buys nothing without raising requestTimeoutMs."}, {"id": "changelog_transport_manager", "label": "Transport manager (scoring, retry, circuit breaker, failover)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retry no longer backs off in front of an open breaker; it moves to the next transport immediately, which is why fallbacks exist."}, {"id": "changelog_peer_identity_split", "label": "Peer id split into mailbox address and identity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.3.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A short-lived session can take its own address without losing who it is; allowPeers now matches configured peerId."}, {"id": "changelog_git_transport", "label": "git transport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Push only counts as published once the commit is on the remote-tracking branch (lost 10/50 requests otherwise). Second runtime on one workDir clones into <workDir>.peers/ because git does not support shared working trees. Never takes over a parent checkout."}, {"id": "changelog_github_transport", "label": "github transport (gh CLI)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_filesystem_transport", "label": "filesystem transport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_memory_transport", "label": "memory transport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_envelope_encryption", "label": "AES-256-GCM envelope encryption", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "changelog_object_key_layout", "label": "Readable object keys ws/<workspace>/inbox/<peer>/<id>.ddf", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately clear text so an operator can understand a repository; earlier README/0.1.0 claims that names never appear in clear text were false and corrected."}, {"id": "changelog_at_least_once_delivery", "label": "At-least-once delivery over object storage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Delete-as-acknowledgement, redelivery with backoff, dedup; handlers must be safe to run twice."}, {"id": "changelog_version_module", "label": "Version read from package manifest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hard-coded 0.1.0 literal leaked into ddrop status and /health; a test now fails the build on any hard-coded version."}, {"id": "changelog_e2e_script", "label": "scripts/e2e.sh (fast and live tiers)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}], "edges": [{"source": "changelog", "target": "changelog_fyrlabs_dead_drop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog", "target": "changelog_transport_sdk", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_fyrlabs_dead_drop", "target": "changelog_transport_sdk", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_transport_sdk", "target": "changelog_deaddroperror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_transport_sdk", "target": "changelog_conformance_suite", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.6.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_transport_manager", "target": "changelog_deaddroperror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_eslint_layering", "target": "changelog_fyrlabs_dead_drop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.2.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog", "target": "changelog_streaming_responses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.16.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_streaming_responses", "target": "changelog_response_cap_32mib", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.1.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_streaming_responses", "target": "changelog_proxy_mode", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.8, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.16.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_content_encoding_fix", "target": "changelog_proxy_mode", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.15.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_adaptive_polling", "target": "changelog_git_transport", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.15.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_key_rotation", "target": "changelog_peer_enrollment", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.13.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_key_rotation", "target": "changelog_envelope_encryption", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.8, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.13.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_peer_enrollment", "target": "changelog_ddrop_discover", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 0.9, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": "0.13.0", "weight": 1}, {"source": "changelog_ddrop_init", "target": "changelog_github_transport", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "co